      "id": "s07_revelation",
      "scene": "two_meters",
      "min_duration": 8.0,
      "pad_after": 0.4,
      "narration": "Profit measures what a business earned over a period. Cash flow tracks money actually moving in and out. When the timing slips, even a profitable business can hit trouble. It's not the only way companies fail, but Australian liquidators name cash-flow problems more than any other single cause.",
      "caption": "Profit = earned over a period. Cash flow = money moving in and out.",
